            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "KONWAL"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is awesome! I made with light Miracle Whip. Skipped the onion. I almost added more liquid as it seemed very light on dressing when I made it. Glad that I didn't, however, as it moistened up after sitting in the refrigerator for awhile. I also added some celery seed as we like that in our coleslaw. Will definately make this again. Thanks."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Catherine Stetenfeld"
            },
            "reviewBody": "It was too sweet so I dumped it and started over. Combined everything except the sugar. Then added sugar 1T at a time until the right balance of sweet/sour for our family. I ended up using 2T sugar.",
            "datePublished": "2022-12-02T23:12:17.234Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Anne-Marie"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This is a good starter for what I have since perfected over the years to make it my own :-).\nI cut the sugar down to 2-3 t. (3 teaspoons is plenty-plenty) \nAnd, I add to the recipe... \n1 T. dijon mustard\n1 t. celery seed\n2 t. horseradish\n1/4 C. salted sunflower seeds\n1/4 C. raisins\n1/2 C. chopped fresh, raw broccoli\nAnd, I only use 1 \"Fuji\" apple, chopped\nLastly, I think it tastes much better if marinated a few hours.\nSometimes I can find in the grocery store bags that already have the carrots and broccoli inside.",
            "datePublished": "2018-05-24T15:38:07.633Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Angula"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Added1/8 tsp cayenne pepper to cut sweetness and placed in gallon ziplock for it to marinate.\nawesome tasting will always be my go to recipe",
            "datePublished": "2020-07-25T17:57:53.640Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Dave Bollman"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Excellent, full of flavor does not taste anything like bland KFC. This is in another league of itself. The vinegar and lemon give plenty of tang flavor. If you want a base recipe to tweak this is the goto recipe as all others I have tried don't come close to the flavor of this one. I eventually tweaked used heavy whipping cream, celery seed, and a pinch of cumin. Served this in a restaurant and got rave reviews. Kept sauce and cabbage separate since the sauce will keep about 6 days so when I needed product would mix a 4:3 ratio of cabbage to sauce. The recipe will not disappoint.",
            "datePublished": "2021-08-22T00:10:26.493Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Kirin Lee"
            },
            "reviewBody": "The first time I made this, it was too sweet. It like slaw a bit tangy. I put the dressing in the blender to make it creamier because it seemed lumpy with just the whisk. The second time I made it, I used some blue agave syrup instead of sugar. Worked great. Also, because we don't drink regular milk around here, I used almond milk. You can't tell the difference mixed with the other stuff.",
            "datePublished": "2017-05-11T00:47:40.110Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Sacha Viall"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I had never made coleslaw before, so decided to follow recipe as written except with a much smaller portion of cabbage. I also used half red cabbage. I worried there wouldn't be enough dressing, but it was just right for my 4 cups of cabbage. I didn't have 3 house to chill, but was still great",
            "datePublished": "2023-05-25T09:46:37.546Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "CWOK"
            },
            "reviewBody": "We really liked this recipe a lot. I like the lemon juice and the vinegar combo to balance the sweetness. I did reduce the sugar to 1/4 cup, and I'm glad I did, because that was plenty and I think more would have been too much. I also used a tsp. of onion powder instead of minced onion, but next time I make it I will try it with the minced. Best recipe I've tried. It's aw-some coleslaw for sure!!!",
            "datePublished": "2019-02-05T00:00:19.120Z"
          },
          {
